<title>BELGIUM: Germany wants EU to discuss Bulgarian wheat aid.</title>
<headline>Germany wants EU to discuss Bulgarian wheat aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany has asked EU farm ministers to discuss next week a Bulgarian request for 100,000 tonnes of soft wheat as food aid, an EU official said.</p>
<p>A decision on the Bulgarian request, which follows a poor harvest last year, would normally be taken by the European Commission after being referred to the EU cereals management committee.</p>
<p>EU grain sources said on Monday that the EU could sell Bulgaria between 200,000 and 300,000 tonnes of soft wheat in 1996/97 (July/June).</p>
